<html>
<title>Interval Timer</title>
<body>


<h1>Interval Timer</h1>

<p>
The profiler can also measure a specific time between two triggers. The first time the trigger happens, the timer is started; the second time, it is stopped. The trigger can be setting the Q flag, execution of <code>OUT 1</code> to <code>OUT 7</code> or an interrupt (<code>INT</code>) generation.
</p>

<p>
The trigger type can be set with the <strong>Interval trigger</strong> selector (1) shown below, and the interval time is shown in the <strong>Interval</strong> field (2):
</p>

<p>
<img src="images/profiler_timer.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>
<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>Interval trigger</strong> selector</li>
<li>(2) <strong>Interval</strong> field</li>
</ul>
</body>
</html>
